message.content:
I see the bug. In `HandleDnsRecordResponse`:

```c
char            name[OT_DNS_MAX_NAME_SIZE];
uint8_t         data[kMaxRrDataSize];
...
recordInfo.mDataBuffer     = data;
recordInfo.mDataBufferSize = sizeof(name);   // BUG: should be sizeof(data) = kMaxRrDataSize
```

The `mDataBufferSize` is set to `sizeof(name)` = `OT_DNS_MAX_NAME_SIZE`, but the actual buffer `data` is `kMaxRrDataSize`. If `kMaxRrDataSize < OT_DNS_MAX_NAME_SIZE`, then `OutputBytes(recordInfo.mDataBuffer, recordInfo.mDataBufferSize)` will read beyond the `data` buffer (stack-buffer-overflow READ).

Let me check the sizes.

